{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry and no Integrator feedback yet. I am setting a neutral, well-conditioned baseline rather than tuning to evidence. Five sensors spaced 15 mm apart (x = -0.03 to +0.03) cover about 60 mm across the 25 mm tape, so the line stays in view on bends and during moderate lateral error. A 12 mm footprint gives a good balance: it is larger than the 15 mm spacing's noise-prone small footprint, but small enough to resolve the tape edge. Sensors sit 50 mm ahead of the axle so the reading leads the wheels and gives the controller time to respond. The wheel track (0.12 m) and radius (0.03 m) give a moderate turn authority with enough speed capability for the 1.5 m/s average needed. Body width 0.12 m keeps the off-track limit at the 0.06 m floor. Mass 0.8 kg and a 0.16 m body length give a moderate yaw inertia, so the robot neither lurches nor responds too sluggishly. I expect this baseline to finish the oval and s-bend tracks, with the slalom as the harder test of sensor coverage and response speed.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.03, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.015, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.015, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.03, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "intent": "Baseline symmetric five-sensor array with 15 mm spacing, 12 mm footprints, and sensors 50 mm ahead of the axle. Purpose: a neutral platform that covers the tape across bends and gives the Integrator a clean reference for sensor coverage, lead distance, and drivetrain authority. Expected result: completion on oval and s-bend, with slalom the likeliest failure point. If the robot loses the line on sharp bends, the next step is to widen the array or move sensors further forward.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Does the five-sensor spacing of 15 mm give a clean, monotonic signal across the tape edge, or is there dead zone or saturation at the centre?",
      "Is 50 mm lead distance enough for the controller to respond on the slalom, or does it cause overshoot?",
      "Is the 0.12 m wheel track giving enough turn authority at base speeds near 2.0, or is the robot slipping on bends?",
      "Does the 0.8 kg mass and 0.16 m body length give stable yaw, or does it oscillate?"
    ]
  },
  "learning": "No race evidence yet. Hypotheses to test: (1) a 12 mm footprint with 15 mm spacing gives adequate tape coverage; (2) forward sensor lead of 50 mm reduces line loss on sharp bends; (3) the 0.12 m track and 0.8 kg mass do not limit average speed above 1.5 m/s.",
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor array",
      "notes": "Neutral first geometry: five 12 mm sensors at 15 mm spacing, 50 mm ahead of the axle, on a 0.12 m track and 0.8 kg body. No race evidence exists yet, so this is a reference platform chosen for coverage and stability, and the feedback asks the Integrator to test those choices."
    }
  }
}
